title: 'umbrella: remove test utility crates and generate-bags'
doc:
  - audience:
      - Node Dev
      - Runtime Dev
    description: |
      The `polkadot-sdk` umbrella crate no longer includes `asset-test-utils`,
      `bridge-hub-test-utils`, `emulated-integration-tests-common`,
      `parachains-runtimes-test-utils` and `generate-bags`. The `node` feature enabled these
      crates, but nodes do not use them.

      The test utility crates pulled `assets-common` and `pallet-revive` into each node that
      uses the umbrella. With `runtime-benchmarks`, they also built `pallet-revive-fixtures`.
      `generate-bags` pulled `pallet-staking-async` into each node. With `runtime-benchmarks`,
      `pallet-staking-async` did not compile.

      These crates are still published. If you use them through the umbrella, add them as
      direct dependencies.
crates:
  - name: polkadot-sdk
    bump: major
  - name: asset-test-utils
    bump: none
  - name: bridge-hub-test-utils
    bump: none
  - name: emulated-integration-tests-common
    bump: none
  - name: parachains-runtimes-test-utils
    bump: none
  - name: generate-bags
    bump: none
